{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`no_file_impact_reason` is operator-authored free text in the signed plan-review material. The original whitespace-normalization epic established that insignificant whitespace must not stale attestations while substantive edits must. Runtime proof shows `material_basis()` still hashes this reason raw, so boundary whitespace produces `stale-material`.\n\nCompatibility spans three historical fingerprint generations: pre-330c raw description/raw reason; post-330c pre-2be7 checkbox-normalized/raw reason; and post-2be7 pre-this-fix whitespace-normalized description/raw reason.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Add a held-out in-process RED oracle through the real material fingerprint and attestation-validity seams.\n- Add an independent boolean `normalize_reason` parameter, defaulting `True`, to `material_basis`; thread it through `material_fingerprint` and `current_material_fingerprint_impl`. Normalize insignificant reason whitespace only when this parameter is enabled.\n- In `_legacy_material_ok`, explicitly pass `normalize_reason=False` in EACH historical candidate. Keep the existing pre-330c candidate (`normalize_checkboxes=False`) and post-330c/pre-2be7 candidate (`normalize_whitespace=False`), and add the post-2be7/pre-fix candidate with only `normalize_reason=False`. This makes every raw-reason generation exactly reproducible while the current path uses the default normalized reason.\n- Run the focused plan-review suites, mutation-check the exact raw-reason defect, then run lint, typecheck, and the broader unit gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Boundary/trailing whitespace-only variants of `no_file_impact_reason` produce the same current material fingerprint and a signed review remains `certified`.\n- [ ] Interior whitespace or a word change remains material and yields `stale-material`.\n- [ ] Pre-330c and post-330c/pre-2be7 legacy candidates explicitly disable reason normalization and continue matching their historical raw-reason fingerprints.\n- [ ] Post-2be7/pre-fix attestations with canonical descriptions and raw reasons are grandfathered by the explicit third `normalize_reason=False` candidate.\n- [ ] A valid-looking unrelated fingerprint remains stale, and existing legacy/description-normalization tests pass unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\nFocused pytest nodes cover fingerprint equality, exact validity status, negative controls, and all legacy generations. The final change also passes repository lint, typecheck, and unit-test gates."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786298940056407001,"uuid":"a63d841f-293e-475a-958f-517a2da04bb1"}